@page "/demo/cards"
@using FlexCore.Showcase.Components.Shared
@using FlexCore.Showcase.Data

@* 2026-10-13: new page on FeatureDemoLayout; two examples (card, card group). Facts checked against CardControl.razor(.css),
   CardGroupControl.razor and FlexControlBase.cs (FlexCore 0.2.48). Cards moved here from UI elements. The Razor tabs are
   generated verbatim from the Demo blocks by script. *@
@* 2026-10-25 (SC-347): third example, "carousel": CarouselControl with six CarouselItemControls, each a CardControl for a
   TravelData package. Facts checked against CarouselControl.razor(.css) and CarouselItemControl.razor (FlexCore 0.2.49): the
   methods are Next, Prev and SelectSlide; there is no key handling and no ARIA beyond the buttons' labels, so the example adds
   role, aria-roledescription and aria-label on the root and an aria-live count. The two card examples are unchanged. *@

<PageTitle>Cards — FlexCore Showcase</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Cards" Category="Components" ControlName="CardControl · CardGroupControl · CarouselControl"
                   Tagline="A bordered container with an optional header, image, body and footer, a grid that lays several of them out, and a carousel that shows one at a time."
                   SourcePath="CardControl.razor; CardGroupControl.razor; CarouselControl.razor; CarouselItemControl.razor">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            <code>CardControl</code> stacks four regions: a header from <code>Title</code> and <code>Subtitle</code> (or your own
            <code>HeaderContent</code>), an image from <code>ImageUrl</code>, the body from child content, and a right-aligned
            <code>FooterContent</code> row. <code>Elevation</code> picks one of three shadow depths. <code>CardGroupControl</code> is a
            grid of 280px-minimum columns that wraps as the page narrows and stretches every card in a row to the same height.
            <code>CarouselControl</code> shows one <code>CarouselItemControl</code> at a time, with arrow and dot buttons of its own,
            a two-way <code>ActiveIndex</code> and three public methods for moving from code.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="card" Title="Card with image, header and footer" RazorCode="@Code.Card" CSharpCode="@Code.CardCs">
            <Description><p><code>Title</code> and <code>Subtitle</code> fill the header; the image sits between header and body, and <code>ImageAlt</code> falls back to the title. Footer children line up on the right. Pick an elevation to compare the shadows; 0 leaves only the border.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="demo-row">
                    <span class="field-label">Elevation</span>
                    <ButtonGroupControl Items="_elevationItems" Values="@(new[] { _elevation.ToString() })" ValuesChanged="PickElevation" AriaLabel="Elevation" />
                </div>
                <div class="card-stage">
                    <CardControl Title="EST-2042 Contoso kitchen" Subtitle="Draft · 14 lines" ImageUrl="images/card-kitchen.svg" ImageAlt="Kitchen plan, revision B" Elevation="@_elevation">
                        <ChildContent><p class="m0">Quartz counters, cabinet install and tile backsplash. Last saved today 09:12 by Dana.</p></ChildContent>
                        <FooterContent>
                            <BadgeControl Text="In progress" Variant="BadgeVariant.Success" />
                            <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="@(() => _opened++)">Open</ButtonControl>
                        </FooterContent>
                    </CardControl>
                </div>
                <p class="result">@(_opened == 0 ? "Open has not been clicked." : $"Open clicked {_opened} time{(_opened == 1 ? "" : "s")}.")</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="group" Title="Card group" RazorCode="@Code.Group" CSharpCode="@Code.GroupCs">
            <Description><p>Three cards from a list. <code>HeaderContent</code> replaces the title block, here with an icon. Narrow the window and the grid drops to two columns, then one.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <CardGroupControl>
                    @foreach (var e in _estimates)
                    {
                        <CardControl Elevation="1">
                            <HeaderContent><span class="head"><span class="@e.Icon"></span> @e.Name</span></HeaderContent>
                            <ChildContent><p class="m0">@e.Summary</p></ChildContent>
                            <FooterContent><BadgeControl Text="@e.Status" Variant="@e.Variant" /></FooterContent>
                        </CardControl>
                    }
                </CardGroupControl>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="carousel" Title="Carousel of destination cards" RazorCode="@Code.Carousel" CSharpCode="@Code.CarouselCs" CssCode="@Code.CarouselCss">
            <Description><p>Six packages from the tour catalogue, one card per <code>CarouselItemControl</code>. The arrows and dots are the carousel's own buttons; Previous, Next and First below call its <code>Prev()</code>, <code>Next()</code> and <code>SelectSlide(0)</code>. Every move raises <code>ActiveIndexChanged</code>, which <code>@@bind-ActiveIndex</code> turns into the count. Next and Previous wrap round at the ends. Only the current card is rendered. The switches set <code>ShowNavButtons</code> and <code>ShowIndicators</code>.</p></Description>
            <Controls>
                <SwitchControl @bind-Checked="_showNav" Label="Nav buttons" />
                <SwitchControl @bind-Checked="_showDots" Label="Indicators" />
            </Controls>
            <Demo>
                <CarouselControl @ref="_carousel" @bind-ActiveIndex="_slide" ShowNavButtons="_showNav" ShowIndicators="_showDots"
                                 role="region" aria-roledescription="carousel" aria-label="Destinations">
                    @foreach (var t in _trips)
                    {
                        <CarouselItemControl>
                            <div class="trip-slide">
                                <CardControl Title="@t.City" Subtitle="@t.Country" Elevation="2">
                                    <ChildContent><p class="trip-blurb">@t.Blurb</p></ChildContent>
                                    <FooterContent>
                                        <span class="trip-package">@t.Package</span>
                                        <BadgeControl Text="@($"{t.Nights} nights")" Variant="BadgeVariant.Info" />
                                    </FooterContent>
                                </CardControl>
                            </div>
                        </CarouselItemControl>
                    }
                </CarouselControl>
                <div class="trip-pager">
                    <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="@(() => _carousel!.Prev())">Previous</ButtonControl>
                    <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="@(() => _carousel!.Next())">Next</ButtonControl>
                    <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="@(() => _carousel!.SelectSlide(0))" Disabled="@(_slide == 0)">First</ButtonControl>
                    <span class="trip-count" aria-live="polite">Card @(_slide + 1) of @_trips.Length</span>
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <DocSections>
            <DocSection Id="doc-cardcontrol-parameters" Title="CardControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Card.Length, "parameters")' Open="true">
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="CardControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Card" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-cardgroupcontrol-parameters" Title="CardGroupControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Group.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="CardGroupControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Group" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-css-classes" Title="CSS classes" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Css.Length, "classes")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssClasses" Title="CSS classes" Rows="Vocab.Css" />
                <p>Colours, padding and the three shadows are fixed in the stylesheet; it reads no <code>--fx-*</code> variables. Restyle by overriding these classes.</p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-carouselcontrol-parameters" Title="CarouselControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Carousel.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="CarouselControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Carousel" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-carouselcontrol-events" Title="CarouselControl events" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.CarouselEvents.Length, "events")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Events" Title="CarouselControl events" Rows="Vocab.CarouselEvents" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-carouselcontrol-methods" Title="CarouselControl methods" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.CarouselMethods.Length, "methods")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Methods" Title="CarouselControl methods" Rows="Vocab.CarouselMethods" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-carouselitemcontrol-parameters" Title="CarouselItemControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Item.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="CarouselItemControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Item" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-carouselitemcontrol-properties" Title="CarouselItemControl read-only property" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.ItemProps.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="CarouselItemControl read-only property" Rows="Vocab.ItemProps" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-carousel-css-classes" Title="Carousel CSS classes" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.CarouselCss.Length, "classes")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssClasses" Title="Carousel CSS classes" Rows="Vocab.CarouselCss" />
                <p>The carousel stylesheet reads no <code>--fx-*</code> variables either. The arrows and dots sit over the item, so pad the item's content to keep it clear of them, as the example's CSS does.</p>
            </DocSection>
        </DocSections>
    </Vocabulary>

    <Accessibility>
        <ul>
            <li>A card is a plain <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> with no role. <code>Title</code> renders as an <code>&lt;h5&gt;</code> and <code>Subtitle</code> as an <code>&lt;h6&gt;</code>; use <code>HeaderContent</code> when the page needs a different heading level.</li>
            <li>The image's <code>alt</code> is <code>ImageAlt</code>, then <code>Title</code>, then "Card image". Give decorative images an empty <code>ImageAlt</code>.</li>
            <li>Nothing in a card is focusable except what you put in it. The footer is a flex row, so buttons there keep their natural Tab order.</li>
            <li><code>CardGroupControl</code> is a CSS grid; it adds no list semantics.</li>
            <li><code>CarouselControl</code> renders a plain <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> with no role, no <code>aria-roledescription</code> and no label. The carousel example passes <code>role="region"</code>, <code>aria-roledescription="carousel"</code> and <code>aria-label</code> as attributes, which the control forwards to that div.</li>
            <li>The arrows are buttons labelled "Previous" and "Next"; each dot is a button labelled "Slide 1", "Slide 2" and so on. The current dot is marked only by its <code>active</code> class (solid and wider), with no <code>aria-current</code> or pressed state. The dots are 10px circles, a small target.</li>
            <li>The carousel has no key handling; arrow keys do nothing. Its arrows and dots are native buttons, reached with Tab and pressed with Enter or Space.</li>
            <li>Only the current item is in the page, so the other cards cannot be reached by Tab or by a screen reader until they are shown. The control does not announce a change of slide; the example's count line is <code>aria-live="polite"</code>, so screen readers announce the new position.</li>
        </ul>
    </Accessibility>

    <Related>
        <ul>
            <li>Badges, alerts, skeletons, timeline and breadcrumb: <a href="demo/new-components">UI elements</a>.</li>
            <li>Cards placed on a fixed grid of cells: the dashboard example in <a href="demo/layout#dashboard">Page layouts</a>.</li>
        </ul>
    </Related>
</FeatureDemoLayout>

